      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(tailscale): guard JSON.parse crash in hasTailscaleFunnelRouteForPort",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where `hasTailscaleFunnelRouteForPort` would crash with an unhandled `SyntaxError` when tailscale `funnel status --json` returned malformed JSON. The `parsePossiblyNoisyJsonObject` call was outside the try-catch block that only protected the exec call.\n\nAffects health checks, funnel route detection, and route setup.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nWrap the `parsePossiblyNoisyJsonObject` call in a separate try-catch that returns `false` (same behavior as the exec-failure path). The other two call sites were already protected by their own try-catch blocks.\n\n## User Impact\n\nPrevents unhandled SyntaxError crashes when tailscale outputs malformed funnel status JSON.\n\n## Evidence\n\n**Runtime terminal proof:**\n\n![screenshot](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/zhangLei99586/openclaw/proof-screenshots/pr-98649-proof.png)\n\n- `src/infra/tailscale.test.ts`: 30/30 passed ✅\n- Updated test: `hasTailscaleFunnelRouteForPort gracefully handles malformed JSON output` (was `preserves malformed status parse failures`)\n- All 3 `parsePossiblyNoisyJsonObject` call sites verified guarded at runtime",
        "branch": "fix/tailscale-json-parse-guard",
